(VAL-19: the conditional-value-RETURN limitation — the factorial pattern
 (`If ... return a value, <expr>. Otherwise ...`) in a function whose `To`
 line has no `Return` does not track the return type. Returning a text
 literal from a frame whose parameter was a number prints a stable garbage
 number (4210906) mis-tagged as Number (dynamic). The reverse direction
 (returning a number from a text frame) segfaults — see Discrepancy 1,
 whose minimal repro is D1.vox. The conditional-value-PARAMETER half (void
 return) works fine — also shown here.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox VAL-19.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   kept
   Text (dynamic)
   4210906
   Number (dynamic)
   num
   not num
)
To label with a value called v.
  If v is a text, return a value, v.
  Otherwise, return a value, "fallback".

a value called kept is label of "kept".
print kept.
print kept's type.
a value called lost is label of 9.
print lost.
print lost's type.

To handle with a value called v.
  If v is a number, print "num".
  Otherwise, print "not num".

handle of 5.
handle of "x".
